From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:39:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/25] [Bugfix][Frontend] Keep GLM tool-call markup as content
 without tools

With --enable-auto-tool-choice and the glm47 tool parser, a request that
offers no tools still has its output parsed for <tool_call> blocks:
_is_valid_tool_name accepts any name when the tool list is empty, so the
markup becomes a tool call. The serving layer then drops the tool calls
of a request without tools, and the text the model wrote disappears.

When the request offers no tools, set the engine's skip_tool_parsing so
tool-call markup passes through as literal content (a <tool_call> that
ends reasoning still ends it). Requests with tools, and tool_choice
"none" with tools, behave as before.

Source: knapcio/GLM-5.3-Flash-4x-DGX-Spark-TP4 @ 770d115,
  overlay/glm47_moe.py and overlay/abstract_parser.py ("K6
  literal-no-tools fix", MIT), after logprobz's local-inference-lab/vllm
  #639 and #640. Re-implemented: the source rebuilt the engine config
  without tool terminals from the facade, and also made tool_choice
  "none" literal; this uses the engine's existing skip_tool_parsing flag
  in the GLM parser and leaves "none" to upstream's suppression.
Upstream: absent in v0.31.0 and main.
Claimed gain: correctness only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py b/vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py
index 9a18228fb..dd3716b9a 100644
--- a/vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py
+++ b/vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py
@@ -233,6 +233,16 @@ class Glm47MoeParser(ParserEngine):
         )
         super().__init__(tokenizer, tools, **kwargs)
 
+    def _check_skip_tool_parsing(
+        self,
+        request: ChatCompletionRequest | ResponsesRequest,
+    ) -> None:
+        # With no tools offered, tool-call markup is literal content: there is
+        # nothing it could call, and parsing it would drop the text.
+        if not getattr(request, "tools", None):
+            self.skip_tool_parsing = True
+        super()._check_skip_tool_parsing(request)
+
     def _emit_name_delta(self, idx: int, deltas, name: str | None) -> None:
         if name is not None:
             name = name.strip()
